Per-series build notes for bsh-shell
=====================================

libsecp256k1 ABI by Ubuntu series:

  Noble 24.04         libsecp256k1-1   (source 0.4.x)
  Oracular 24.10      libsecp256k1-2   (source 0.5.x)
  Plucky 25.04        libsecp256k1-2   (source 0.5.x)
  Questing 25.10      libsecp256k1-2   (source 0.5.x)
  26.04 +             libsecp256k1-6   (source 0.6.x)

`Build-Depends: libsecp256k1-dev` resolves to whatever the chroot's
libsecp256k1 happens to be. The runtime dependency is auto-discovered
by dpkg-shlibdeps via `${shlibs:Depends}` and pins to the runtime
SONAME the binary was actually linked against.

Consequence: a .deb built on Plucky declares
`libsecp256k1-2` as its runtime dep and will NOT install on Noble
(which only has libsecp256k1-1). The Launchpad recipe MUST build
separately per target series. Do not copy a single binary across
series.

If a series fails build with a libsecp256k1-dev missing/wrong-version
error, check that the recipe targets that series with its own chroot
and that the chroot's apt index has libsecp256k1-dev for that
release.

brightdate-rust submodule / Launchpad
-------------------------------------

bsh embeds brightdate-rust as a git submodule. Launchpad git checkouts
often do not expand submodules, leaving an empty `brightdate-rust/`
directory or a stale checkout without the pinned release.

`debian/rules` detects a missing `crates/btime/src/color.rs` and then:
  1. runs `git submodule update --init --recursive brightdate-rust`
  2. if still missing, downloads the tag named in
     `debian/brightdate-rust-version` from GitHub

Bump `debian/brightdate-rust-version` whenever the bsh release rebases
onto a new brightdate-rust tag.
